{"hash":"1030282abf380389","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":75.478,"said":"This fierce face of silver, with its wide eyes and great moustache, is Kala Bhairava, and in Kashi he holds a special office. The Puranas tell that Brahma once spoke a falsehood in his pride, and from Shiva’s anger Bhairava appeared and struck off Brahma’s fifth head. But to strike Brahma was one of the greatest of sins, and the skull clung to Bhairava’s hand. He wandered the worlds with it, and nothing could free him, until he set foot in Kashi, the city of liberation, where at last the skull fell from his hand. The place is remembered as Kapal Mochan, the release of the skull. So Bhairava stayed, as the Kotwal of Kashi, its guardian and the keeper of its order. People say no one may live in Kashi, or truly arrive here, without his leave, and many pilgrims go to his own great temple in the city, the Kaal Bhairav Mandir, to ask it. Devotees bring him mustard oil, black sesame and a black thread to tie on. And see who waits at his feet: his dog, his vahana.\n\nDid you know? The great Kaal Bhairav Mandir stands in the city, near Vishweshwarganj; this is the small shrine within the temple complex.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":970},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":986,"end":1109}],"words":[[0.098,0.264,0,4],[0.374,0.373,5,11],[0.759,0.3,12,16],[1.072,0.12,17,19],[1.204,0.493,20,26],[1.937,0.168,28,32],[2.117,0.168,33,36],[2.298,0.325,37,41],[2.634,0.3,42,46],[2.947,0.12,47,50],[3.079,0.3,51,56],[3.391,0.601,57,66],[4.245,0.168,68,70],[4.425,0.312,71,75],[4.75,0.517,76,84],[5.531,0.156,86,89],[5.699,0.108,90,92],[5.819,0.433,93,98],[6.264,0.132,99,101],[6.408,0.349,102,107],[6.769,0.084,108,109],[6.865,0.481,110,117],[7.358,0.517,118,124],[8.762,0.108,126,129],[8.882,0.589,130,137],[9.483,0.264,138,142],[9.76,0.144,143,147],[9.916,0.385,148,154],[10.312,0.337,155,159],[10.661,0.288,160,165],[10.962,0.06,166,167],[11.034,0.565,168,177],[11.611,0.108,178,180],[11.73